# Test: an external command module with an unserved ze:command node is refused at Stage 1 and by the conformance checker
#
# Question: when an external plugin brings a valid -cmd module whose
# `show acme-monitor target` ze:command node is reached by no command the plugin
# declares at Stage 1, does `ze show plugin conformance run` refuse it offline
# under `command-nodes-served` naming the node and the module, and does
# `ze start` refuse the plugin at Stage 1 with the same refusal and fail startup
# without ever reaching `Ze running.`?
# Why not a unit test: TestStage1RefusesACommandNodeNoDeclaredCommandReaches
# (internal/component/plugin/server/stage1_commands_test.go) and
# TestRunJudgesTheCommandNodesOfTheDeclaredModules (conformance) prove the check
# in isolation. Only the real binaries prove that the shipped daemon joins the
# command module cleanly at boot, then refuses the plugin at its startup tier's
# Stage 1 and aborts startup, and that `ze show plugin conformance run` reports
# the same failure from the CLI.
#
# The fixture's command-unserved variant
# (internal/test/fixture/plugin_fixture_external_yang.go) brings Valid,
# Commands and API, and declares only `show acme-monitor status` at Stage 1,
# leaving `show acme-monitor target` unserved. Its stage1Refused flag turns a
# ready daemon into ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-40 of spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup (narrowed): both the
#   live Stage 1 refusal at `ze start` and the offline conformance check.
# PREVENTS: an external plugin publishing a ze:command node in the command tree
#   that no declared command serves, which would leave operators seeing a
#   command that fails with "not registered" when invoked.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT

tmpfs=unserved.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external unserved-command {
		run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang command-unserved"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Step 1: offline conformance check refuses the plugin under command-nodes-served.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "le test fixture plugin/external-yang command-unserved" name unserved-command:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=command-nodes-served
expect=stdout:contains=fail
expect=stdout:contains=show acme-monitor target
expect=stdout:contains=acme-monitor-cmd

# Step 2: ze start joins the modules, then refuses the plugin at Stage 1 and
# aborts the startup tier without reaching "Ze running.".
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze start unserved.conf:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=unserved-command
expect=stderr:contains=show acme-monitor target
expect=stderr:contains=acme-monitor-cmd
expect=stderr:contains=declares no command at Stage 1 that reaches it
reject=stderr:contains=Ze running.
reject=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: external-yang generation 1 ready
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
